# Git commits — single author only

Cursor injects `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` when using `git commit`. **Never use `git commit`** for this project.

Use `git commit-tree` instead so commits list only **Jefferson Wu** as author:

```bash
export GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="Jefferson Wu"
export GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="jeffersonw888@gmail.com"
export GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="Jefferson Wu"
export GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="jeffersonw888@gmail.com"

git add <files>
TREE=$(git write-tree)
PARENT=$(git rev-parse HEAD)
NEW=$(git commit-tree "$TREE" -p "$PARENT" -m "commit message here")
git update-ref HEAD "$NEW"
```

Verify before push: `git cat-file -p HEAD` must **not** contain `Co-authored-by`.

# Unit test construction

In `src/test/java/domain/*Tests.java`, only the **class under test** may be constructed with `new`. All collaborators (Territory, Player when testing another class, GameMap, DeckManager, Random, RiskCard, etc.) must be EasyMock mocks/stubs.
